{
 "notes": {
  "what": "Every scheduler configuration of the lease campaign (tools/campaign.py documents the format). A configuration id is <family>.<system>.<knob>; the lease rows in configs/scope.json pick which ones run.",
  "weights": "The eight RouteBalance weight vectors of the v3 grid (p1_pareto.sh RB_WEIGHTS), each summing to 1 exactly: uniform is 1/3 each (v3's 0.33 summed to 0.99, which the config now rejects).",
  "rb": "rb = the G1 candidate default (D16): profiled TPOT(running batch) + batch_aware envelope + fixed_ref normalization. rb-static = the v3-like static arm: constant TPOT + queue_aware + max_divide (plan section 1 ablations). Both read the W1 table (D37: one calibration run gives the curve and the constant).",
  "ablations": "abl-* are W4's arms (D41), each the rb configuration with the one change its name says (and only what that change forces): lpt-off; round1 / round32 (fixed rounds); xgb (the learned heads retrained on the W1b sweep; the xgboost source pairs only with queue_aware); wlat0 (v2 arm 2: w_latency = 0, the reactive shortest-queue tie-break); static-prior (v2 arm 4: constant TPOT x own length, queue-blind); prompt-blind (per-model mean prior, D10); half-labels (the 50%-label KNN index); dr-off (dead reckoning off); maxdiv (the normalization arm: the curve with max_divide); wq0 / wc0 (per-term drops). Dropped weights are rescaled so the rest sum to 1, which leaves every argmax unchanged. v2's arm 3 (w_latency = 0 with a predictive argmin tie-break) is dropped (owner 09-25): the rebuilt tie-break is fixed (D35). const-batch is the D45 control (constant TPOT in the batch_aware envelope); it runs (owner 09-25). abl-lpt-min / abl-lpt-mean are W11 (LPT key min / mean, D41; the configuration accepts them from S5b on). Each template's ablates lists the manifest paths its arm changes from the rb reference (the parity gate checks it differs in exactly those).",
  "baselines": "AvengersPro: upstream's route-time defaults, top_k 1 and beta 9.0 (its config.py, which also sets the artifacts' 32 clusters; D89; v3 ran top_k 4 for Qwen / 3 for Gemma and beta 5.0), the MiniLM embedder at the pinned revision (the same as the KNN encoder's), the upstream checkout pinned by digest (dfb60b1 plus the local patch that makes its training-only datasets import optional). BEST-Route as its authors ship it (D79): upstream's ranker (microsoft/best-route-llm fc9b896, train_router.py, loss prob_nlabels, DeBERTa-v3-small) trained per family on the rebuilt rows, served by upstream's code; a request goes to the cheapest model (fleet price order, D71) whose score P(as good as the reference) - P(worse) is at least the threshold, 0 / 0.3 / 0.5 / 0.7; the reference (the family's largest model) always qualifies. The part br.router.v3 is v3's 4-way classifier recipe, the owner's backup (pin br-v3.<family>). Dispatchers: round robin, power of two, least outstanding (the engine's running + waiting: v3's shortest queue, D40), random, lowest_latency with LiteLLM's 10-sample window (D25). Every pipeline system reads the engines' own counts, never dead reckoning (RouteBalance's mechanism, owner 09-25); the appendix row's disp.*-inflight presets count their own in-flight requests instead (D84). Ties go to the least recently used instance (D35, in the code).",
  "telemetry": "How each system reads load (telemetry_read; D53, D54, D55, D61, D84, owner 09-25/26). RouteBalance fetches every instance once per batch (per_round), with dead reckoning, its own mechanism. The pipeline systems never use dead reckoning; their load-reading dispatchers (least-outstanding, power of two) count the engines' own running and waiting gauges (count engine): from the background pollers' 50 ms cache (poll), as llm-d's endpoint picker scrapes each model server's /metrics every 50 ms, in the main grid; or fetched for every request (per_request), as v3's baselines did (the *-probe presets, the day-1 check; the probes fetch the router's candidates). The disp.*-inflight presets (the appendix row W12, D84) count each instance's in-flight requests instead, as Envoy's LEAST_REQUEST and NGINX's least_conn count at the proxy. rb-poll and rb-static-poll are RouteBalance on the same pollers' cache (D54)",
  "sweep": "sweep.random is the W1b latency sweep (D38): passthrough router, random dispatch over every instance, pending_decode own_length, so the server writes latency.<digest>.jsonl. It runs with dead reckoning, unlike every baseline: it records the learned heads' training features, and RouteBalance serves the heads on dead-reckoned counts (its random dispatch reads no load, so only what is logged changes). Its estimator (parts.estimator.sweep) is the owner's: the sweep sends training-split prompts, and the main KNN index holds every one of them, so its neighbours would include each prompt itself (weight ~1e6 at distance 0) and the logged lengths would be near-exact, unlike at serving on evaluation prompts (a train/serve skew for the learned heads, D38/D43). Options: the main index anyway, or an index built without the sweep's prompts.",
  "decoupled": "RB-decoupled follows the RouteBalance arm it is the control of (same predictors, plan section 1): rb-dec uses the curve arm's latency, rb-static-dec the static arm's; the main grid runs <rb_default>-dec.",
  "pipeline": "In a pipeline configuration the RouteBalance-only keys (rounds, lpt, and for AvengersPro, BEST-Route and dispatcher rows the estimator and latency) are inert: the scheduler does not load or read them. They still enter the configuration digest, so they name the deployment's own artifacts.",
  "budget": "budget.off: admission_filter false in every configuration but the budget sweep's. budget.filter (W7b): v3's budget filter as its budget sweep ran it (routebalance/schedule/assign.py Admission: the expected cost within the budget, else the cheapest by worst-case cost); every system in a budget cell clamps its output to the request's budget (routebalance/schedule/budget.py).",
  "owner": "Owner values (09-25): telemetry poll_ms / timeout_s = 50 / 1.0 (D30; max_age_ms removed, D133); RouteBalance pending_decode = own_length (D31); dispatcher seed 1 (v3's po2 seed); the fixed 32-request round's timeout 200 ms (the adaptive rule pairs 32 with 200 ms). The W1b sweep estimator is the main KNN index (owner 09-25: the sweep measures decode latency across batch shapes; the training prompts are fine for it)",
  "lodo": "D93 (owner 09-27, optional W13): estimator.lodo.<source> is the main index without that source dataset's training rows (knn-lodo-<source>.<family>, one pin per source)",
  "pins": "$pin names come from the lease (tools/campaign.py render --pins): knn.<family> and knn-half.<family> (index dir + md5), tpot-table.<family> (the W1 calibration table + md5), prefill-table.<family> (the prefill lines fitted on W1's single-request level by tools/fit_prefill.py + md5, D118; in every latency part), xgb-heads.<family> (the W1b-trained heads dir + the md5 of its md5s.json), ap.<family>.<pw> (artifact dir), br.<family> (checkpoint dir)."
 },
 "lists": {
  "all_families": ["qwen", "gemma"],
  "qwen_only": ["qwen"],
  "rb_weights": ["q10l10c80", "q10l80c10", "q20l20c60", "q20l60c20", "uniform", "q50l30c20", "q60l20c20", "q80l10c10"],
  "ap_pw": ["pw025", "pw039", "pw053", "pw070", "pw080"],
  "br_t": ["t00", "t03", "t05", "t07"],
  "routed_dispatch": ["lor", "rr", "po2"],
  "probe_dispatch": ["lor", "po2"],
  "rb_arms": ["rb", "rb-static", "rb-learned"],
  "dispatchers": ["rr", "po2", "lor", "random", "lowest-latency"],
  "lodo_sources": ["beaver_tails", "code_ultra_feedback", "gsm8k", "lmsys", "mix_instruct", "reward_bench", "squad"]
 },
